<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch6-chapter-ht-1p-evaluate" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Evaluating Hypotheses</title>

  <introduction>
    <p> This chapter covers the evaluate step of the model-simulate-evaluate process used
        for simulation-based hypothesis testing. Students will learn about p-values and the standardized value of 
        the statistic/Z-score/test statistic. The chapter ends with a discussion on significance level and decision errors.
      </p>
  </introduction>


  <objectives>
    <ol>
    <li>Numerically measure the strength of evidence against the null hypothesis using standardized statistics (Z-scores) and p-values.</li>

    <li>Interpret standardized statistics and p-values, demonstrating an understanding of what these measures can and can not tell you. </li>

    <li>Use Z-scores and p-values to make decisions concerning hypothesis tests.</li>

    <li>Understand the types of errors that can occur with hypothesis testing, their importance, and how they likelihood is related to the level of significance.</li>

  </ol>
  </objectives>

  
  <!-- include sections -->
  <xi:include href="section-ch6-quantify-evidence.ptx" />
  <xi:include href="section-ch6-decision-errors.ptx" />


</chapter>